      "message": "To be honest, I\u0027m not sure what the value of this test is. We need to answer the question: What behavior is verified with this?\n\nIn it\u0027s current form, we are only looking for some very specific substrings in the output, which tests that a few of the fields are output correctly, without checking for consistent/correct formatting.\n\nOne option would be to check the entire output against a literal string, but that would be merely a \"change detector\" test. I don\u0027t think we need or want that.\n\nAnother extreme would be to parse the output and assert its validity. I think that is a lot more complicated than it is worth.\n\nThat leaves us with the question of whether we should have a unit tests for dump()...",
